          %h2#mathematically_inclined_monographs_about_string_theory Mathematically inclined monographs about string theory
          %p There is to date no textbook on string theory genuinely digestible by the standard pure mathematician. Even those that claim to be are not, as experience shows. But here are some books that make a strong effort to go beyond the vagueness of the “mainstream” books, which are listed further below.
          %ul
            %li#Cheng13
              %p
                Miranda Cheng,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Mathematical tools for string theorists
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "http://www.math.jussieu.fr/~chengm/lecture_notes/Thalys_School.pdf"} pdf
              %p
                This is an elementary set of lecture notes introducing the required basics of
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differential+geometry"} differential geometry
                ending with
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2d+CFT"} 2d CFT
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Witten+genus"} Witten genus
                and
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/orbifolds"} orbifolds
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Pierre+Deligne"}> Pierre Deligne
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Pavel+Etingof"} Pavel Etingof
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Dan+Freed"} Dan Freed
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/David+Kazhdan"} David Kazhdan
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/John+Morgan"} John Morgan
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Edward+Witten"} Edward Witten
                (eds).
                = succeed "," do
                  %em
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Quantum+Fields+and+Strings"}> Quantum Fields and Strings
                    , A course for mathematicians
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "http://www.math.ias.edu/qft"} web version
              %p This is a long collection of (in parts) long lectures by many top string theorists and also by some genuine top mathematicians. Correspondingly it covers a lot of ground, while still being introductory. Especially towards the beginning there is a strong effort towards trying to formalize or at least systematize much of the standard lore. But one can see that eventually the task of doing that throughout had been overwhelming. Nevertheless, this is probably the best source that there is out there. If you only ever touch a single book on string theory, touch this one.
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Leonardo+Castellani"}> Leonardo Castellani
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Riccardo+D%27Auria"} Riccardo D'Auria
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Pietro+Fre"} Pietro Fre
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Supergravity+and+Superstrings+-+A+Geometric+Perspective"} Supergravity and Superstrings - A Geometric Perspective
              %p
                This focuses on the discussion of
                = succeed "-aspects" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/supergravity"} supergravity
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/D%27Auria-Fre+formulation+of+supergravity"} D'Auria-Fre formulation of supergravity
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/connection+on+an+infinity-bundle"} infinity-connections
                with values in
                = succeed "s" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/super+L-infinity+algebra"} super L-infinity algebra
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/supergravity+Lie+3-algebra"} supergravity Lie 3-algebra
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hisham+Sati"}> Hisham Sati
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Urs+Schreiber"} Urs Schreiber
                = succeed "," do
                  %em
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/schreiber/show/Mathematical+Foundations+of+Quantum+Field+and+Perturbative+String+Theory"} Mathematical Foundations of Quantum Field and Perturbative String Theory
              %p
                This volume tries to give an impression of the rather recent massive progress that has happened in the mathematical understanding of fundamental ingredients of perturbative string theory, revolving around the proof of the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cobordism+hypothesis"} cobordism hypothesis
                and related topics of
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/higher+category+theory+and+physics"} higher category theory and physics
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Igor+Dolgachev"}> Igor Dolgachev
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Introduction to string theory for mathematicians
                %em
                  %a{:href => "https://people.sissa.it/~bruzzo/sagp99/sagp.html"} 1999 Summer on Algebraic Geometry and Physics
                (1999) &amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "https://dept.math.lsa.umich.edu/~idolga/stringy.pdf"}> pdf
                ,
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/files/Dolgachev-IntroductionStringTheory.pdf", :title => "pdf"} pdf
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Paul+Aspinwall"}> Paul Aspinwall
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Tom+Bridgeland"} Tom Bridgeland
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Michael+Douglas"} Michael Douglas
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Dirichlet branes and mirror symmetry
          %p See also
          %ul
